b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ HARNESS POSING incremental;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE author: implementation-algol-60, an agent (Claude Opus 5.5, claude-opus-5-5);
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE precursor seen: no;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE idioms: the Revised Report on ALGOL 60 (1962) for assignment statements (4.2), arrays (5.2), procedures (5.4), the for statement with a while element (4.6) and conditional statements (4.5), the X1 system's input and output procedures read, PRINTTEXT and NLCR, as the harness README gives them (harnesses/algol-60/README.md, 2.1), and the X1 compiler's representation, with underlined reserved words and the operator symbols (harness README, 2.1), atoms as integer codes (systems file, Values), a program that reads each stage as it arrives, which counts as the same computation (systems file, The same computation), and the message loop and observe block of the harness README example X01 (harnesses/algol-60/README.md, 2.8);
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ CONSTANTS a line k for every stage k: the message the stage brings, as one code, 1 for INC and 2 for READ. The READ messages bind the unknowns r1, r2, r3 and so on, in the order they arrive;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ P14a, and P14c, which is its stages and two more. The counter is implemented as a process holding its count, which the problem allows as a transcription: the program itself, which reads each message as it arrives and answers before it reads the next. The count is the integer variable count, 0 at first, as the messages are posed with run(m, 0). Each message is taken by the case of run for its head, in the order the messages arrive. Case 2: INC, and the rest is run with count + 1, so count becomes count + 1. Case 3: READ(r), with r = count, and the rest is run with count, so r is given the count and count is unchanged. Case 1, run of the empty sequence, would close the stream, and no stage closes it. A message that is neither INC nor READ has no case of run, so run has no solution from that message on. The unknowns r1, r2 and so on are an integer array, at most 1000 of them, fixed in one place;
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ n, cap, m, i, code, k, msg, count, nr, run2, run3;
  b̲o̲o̲l̲e̲a̲n̲ failed;
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ a̲r̲r̲a̲y̲ rv[1:1000];

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ num(v);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ v; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ v;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ output adapter: an integer, a minus sign if it is negative and then its decimal digits, with no spaces;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ d;
    i̲f̲ v < 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`-'); num(-v) e̲n̲d̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      i̲f̲ v ≥ 10 t̲h̲e̲n̲ num(v ÷ 10);
      d := v - v ÷ 10 × 10;
      i̲f̲ d = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`0') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 1 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`1') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`2')
      e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 3 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`3') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 4 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`4') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 5 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`5')
      e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 6 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`6') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 7 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`7') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 8 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`8')
      e̲l̲s̲e̲ PRINTTEXT(`9')
    e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲ num;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ receive(msg);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ msg; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ msg;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the counter receives one message: the case of run for the message at the head of the stream;
  i̲f̲ ¬failed t̲h̲e̲n̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲f̲ msg = 1 t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ case 2: run(the sequence of INC alone ++ s, c) if run(s, c + 1);
      run2 := run2 + 1;
      count := count + 1
    e̲n̲d̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ msg = 2 t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ case 3: run(the sequence of READ(r) alone ++ s, c) if r = c and run(s, c);
      run3 := run3 + 1;
      nr := nr + 1;
      rv[nr] := count
    e̲n̲d̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ no case of run has this message at its head;
      failed := t̲r̲u̲e̲
    e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲ receive;

  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ harness words: the instance line;
  n := read; cap := read; m := read;
  f̲o̲r̲ i := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ m d̲o̲ code := read;
  count := nr := run2 := run3 := 0;
  failed := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲;

  f̲o̲r̲ i := 1 w̲h̲i̲l̲e̲ t̲r̲u̲e̲ d̲o̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ harness words: one message, and the stage it poses;
    code := read; k := read;
    c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the stage's constant: the message the counter receives;
    msg := read;
    receive(msg);

    c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the answer: every unknown a READ has bound so far;
    i̲f̲ ¬failed t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      PRINTTEXT(`[answer]');
      i̲f̲ nr = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`no unknowns')
      e̲l̲s̲e̲
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
        i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ j;
        f̲o̲r̲ j := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ nr d̲o̲
        b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
          PRINTTEXT(`r'); num(j); PRINTTEXT(` = '); num(rv[j]);
          i̲f̲ j < nr t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`, ')
        e̲n̲d̲
      e̲n̲d̲;
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/answer]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲
    e̲n̲d̲;

    c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ observe: the count held, the unknowns bound, and the applications of each case of run;
    PRINTTEXT(`[observe]');
    i̲f̲ failed t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`no solution: a message with no case of run'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
    PRINTTEXT(`count '); num(count); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`, held in the running program, which waits on its next message'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ j;
      f̲o̲r̲ j := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ nr d̲o̲
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[bind r'); num(j); PRINTTEXT(`]'); num(rv[j]); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/bind]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲ e̲n̲d̲
    e̲n̲d̲;
    PRINTTEXT(`[operations run/2 '); num(run2); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
    PRINTTEXT(`[operations run/3 '); num(run3); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/observe]'); NLCR; PRINTTEXT(`[end]') e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲
e̲n̲d̲
